A||||10||86ttops||Where is the MAT Sensor?????||||5||
Z||000000||86ttops||08-16-2001||06:05 PM||||Ok i am getting different answers to the same question from people I know.  Where is the MAT sensor and what does it do.  I have had people tell me it is in the air cleaner and others said it should be screwed into the intake.||||reg||5
Z||000001||c m west||08-16-2001||06:42 PM||||if a V-6 it is located in the air filter canister - 2 wire sensor. for removal use 2 wrenches so as not to break the bung off the canister. Its job is to relay the intake temperature to the computer||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-16-2001||06:49 PM||||its on far driver side of air filter canister like west says. Lots of people (even Autozone) get it confused with MAP sensor.<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-16-2001||07:26 PM||||V6 it's listed as an Air Charge Temp sensor in most parts books and it's in the air cleaner.<P>87-88 4 cyl it's in the intake manifold to the right of the TBI. Some books list it as MAT ofthers as ACT. There are notes about this in several articles in my cave. the longest mention is in the DIS notes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||08-16-2001||07:38 PM||||Also known as Intake Air Temp sensor, or IAT.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bluebottlejunky||08-16-2001||07:54 PM||||and, what is its purpose? I mean MAT manifold air temp..and if this sensor is bad how will it affect the car?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B><p>[This message has been edited by Bluebottlejunky (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rodmcneill||08-17-2001||12:25 AM||||If I remember right when the intake air temp is cooler the ECM enrichens the air fuel mixture, as the MAT sensor warms up the voltage signal changes(resistance) and the mixture is leaned out. When a MAT sensor goes bad usually it is to the lean side so your engine may not be producing its normal power. MAT sensors are cheap and easy to replace. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||07:52 AM||||whereas, MAP (manifold absolute pressure)sensor going bad will make your car run like total crap.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bluebottlejunky||08-17-2001||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>If I remember right when the intake air temp is cooler the ECM enrichens the air fuel mixture, as the MAT sensor warms up the voltage signal changes(resistance) and the mixture is leaned out. When a MAT sensor goes bad usually it is to the lean side so your engine may not be producing its normal power. MAT sensors are cheap and easy to replace. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmm <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">, Sounds just like my car now power when I put her to the floor! Thanks<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||08-17-2001||07:59 PM||||MAP and MAT are both in my cave. DIS notes.||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnF||08-18-2001||07:49 AM||||Yes, Auto Zone gets it confused with the MAP.  Also, Auto Zone cannot special order an IAT.  Anyone know where to get one for a 4 holer?||||reg||1
